-- check/bad: `equatable_outside_core`. The marker is the one spelling in
-- the language user code may not write (checker.md Appendix B): once on a
-- type variable, once as a declaration modifier. Note the `foreign` error
-- rides along, which is the same rule from the other side.
pub eq : equatable a, a, a → Bool
eq a b = True


pub equatable foreign type Handle
